WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.377
Hi, I'm Eyelet!

00:00:02.377 --> 00:00:06.724
This attention layer trains with extra parts, then folds them away, so

00:00:06.724 --> 00:00:08.897
you serve ordinary grouped query attention.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:14.159
The idea: keep two key value heads and half the query heads.

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:16.922
Add two small linear maps to win quality back.

00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:18.764
Then multiply them into the weights.

00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.777
Start with eight physical query heads, half the usual count.

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:27.383
Premix gives each key value group its own matrix.

00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:31.631
Every query head goes through both, so eight become sixteen virtual heads.

00:00:32.051 --> 00:00:35.229
Each group of eight virtual heads attends over one cached head.

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:36.673
The cache holds just two.

00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:40.398
Postmix adds a small low rank mix across the head outputs, so

00:00:40.398 --> 00:00:41.775
the two groups can share.

00:00:43.192 --> 00:00:44.316
Here is the formula.

00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:46.575
Neither map is nonlinear.

00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:48.996
A query head times a Premix matrix...

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:52.639
is the input times their product, which you compute once.

00:00:52.639 --> 00:00:55.539
The same move pushes Postmix into the output weights.

00:00:57.192 --> 00:01:00.729
As trained, the layer has eight query heads and two extra maps.

00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:05.536
As served, it is stock grouped query attention with sixteen query heads

00:01:05.536 --> 00:01:06.816
and two cached heads.

00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:07.775
No new kernel.

00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:12.661
At the paper's one point seven billion shape, that is one kilobyte

00:01:12.661 --> 00:01:15.933
per token per layer, a quarter of the eight head setup.

00:01:17.092 --> 00:01:19.030
I ran the fold at that shape.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.797
In double precision the two graphs agree to round off.

00:01:21.797 --> 00:01:24.012
With a gate after Postmix, they do not.

00:01:25.808 --> 00:01:29.366
So: the fold is exact, and the cache is four times smaller.

00:01:29.366 --> 00:01:32.034
The quality margins are small and from single runs.

00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:33.220
Call it a match.

00:01:34.525 --> 00:01:38.396
Premix makes virtual queries, both maps fold away, and you serve

00:01:38.396 --> 00:01:39.803
plain grouped query attention.

00:01:40.223 --> 00:01:42.262
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:42.262 --> 00:01:42.845
I'm Eyelet.

00:01:42.845 --> 00:01:43.137
Bye!
